{{!
    @template tool_lp/user_summary

    A person, as a chip: avatar, name and identity fields, overridden by Dimensions.

    Mirrors tool_lp/user_summary of Moodle 5.3 (2026100500), admin/tool/lp/templates/user_summary.mustache.
    Re-diff it against that file on every core upgrade. It is included by the evidence summary (the
    person who acted) and by the user competency summary in a course (the learner).

    Kept from core: one link to the profile around the picture, the name and the identity, every key
    double-stashed as core does, and the picture's empty alt (the name beside it is the link's text).
    Changed: the chip's classes (dim-comp-user), a round avatar at 28px in place of core's 18px height.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * profileurl - the profile's address
    * profileimageurlsmall - a small profile picture
    * fullname - the person's full name
    * hasidentity - whether there are identity fields to show
    * identity - the identity fields, concatenated

    Example context (json):
    {
        "id": "2",
        "fullname": "Tess Teacher",
        "hasidentity": true,
        "identity": "tess@example.com",
        "profileurl": "https://example.com/user/profile.php?id=2",
        "profileimageurlsmall": "https://example.com/pix/u/f2.png"
    }
}}
<a class="dim-comp-user" href="{{profileurl}}">
    <img class="dim-comp-user__avatar" height="28" width="28" src="{{profileimageurlsmall}}" alt="">
    <span class="dim-comp-user__name">{{fullname}}</span>
    {{#hasidentity}}
    <small class="dim-comp-user__identity">{{identity}}</small>
    {{/hasidentity}}
</a>
